  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "D_n=n!\\sum_{k=0}^{n}\\frac{(-1)^k}{k!},\\quad \\left|\\frac{D_n}{n!}-e^{-1}\\right|\\le \\frac{1}{(n+1)!},\\quad \\frac{D_n}{n!}\\to e^{-1}.",
    "plain": "Backfill the derangement convergence metadata around the exact inclusion-exclusion formula and quantitative convergence to `1/e`. The Lean support proves derangement counts, alternating-factorial expansions, explicit error bounds, and nearest-integer consequences, with a few older sibling files retaining sorries.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Derangements are the canonical fixed-point-free permutation count.",
      "The `D_n/n! -> 1/e` limit links finite combinatorics to analytic estimates.",
      "The quantitative error bounds support nearest-integer and convergence-rate statements."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "`numDerangements_formula` gives the exact inclusion-exclusion formula.",
      "`derangements_div_factorial` rewrites `D_n/n!` as a finite alternating reciprocal-factorial sum.",
      "`derangements_rate_scaled`, `derangements_nearest_integer`, and `derangements_unique_nearest` prove nearest-integer and scaled error statements in the zero-sorry OQ-01-OQ-01 file.",
      "`derangements_quarter_bound`, `derangements_parametric_bound`, and `derangements_error_sign` provide explicit quantitative refinements."
    ],
    "open": [
